    {
      "text": "New Brunn--Minkowski and functional inequalities via convexity of entropy — We study the connection between the concavity properties of a measure ν and the convexity properties of the associated\n\n**New Brunn--Minkowski and functional inequalities via convexity of entropy**\n\n*GAUTAM AISHWARYA AND LIRAN ROTEM*\n\n32 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We study the connection between the concavity properties of a measure ν and the convexity properties of the associated relative entropy D(·∥ν) along optimal transport. As a corollary we prove a new dimensional Brunn–Minkowski inequality for centered star-shaped bod- ies, when the measure ν is log-concave with a p-homogeneous potential (such as the Gaussian measure). Our method allows us to go beyond the usual convexity assumption on the sets that is fundamentally essential for the standard differential-geometric technique in this area. We then take a finer look at the convexity properties of the Gauss- ian relative entropy, which yields new functional inequalities. First we obtain curvature and dimensional reinforcements to Otto–Villani’s HWI inequality in Gauss space, when restricted to even strongly log-concave measures.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Improved Brunn–Minkowski inequalities; 1.2 Weighted Brunn–Minkowski inequalities for ; 1.3 Towards the best possible exponent in the ; 1.4 Functional Inequalities; Some notation and conventions:; 2 Optimal transport, entropy, and an overview ; 3 Dimensional convexity properties of relative; 4 Dimensional convexity properties of the Gaus; 5 Applications to functional inequalities; References",
      "lang": "en",
